 1138:                // verts on a 316² map at 43k tiles) — we must only invalidate it
 1139:                // when terrain GEOMETRY actually changes.
 1140:                //
 1141:                // PERF (per-frame rebuild storm fix): we previously gated on
 1142:                // HasDirtyTiles, which includes the COLOR + TEXTURE queues. On a
 1143:                // live world the simulation (water flow, fire, lava, mob tints)
 1144:                // re-enqueues color/texture updates for visible tiles EVERY frame,
 1145:                // so HasDirtyTiles was effectively always true → MarkDirty every
 1146:                // frame → a full ~5s geometry rebuild every frame = the storm seen
 1147:                // in Player.log. Terrain SHAPE only changes when a tile's elevation
 1148:                // (scale) changes, so gate the geometry rebuild on HasDirtyHeights
 1149:                // (the scale queue) alone. Color churn no longer triggers a rebuild;
 1150:                // it is consumed by RefreshColors into the GPU color buffer.
 1151:                bool hadDirtyHeights = Manager.HasDirtyHeights;
