  368:            // --- 3. Blended weights: own bone + parent, inverse-distance -------
  369:            // Single-bone rigid weights leave a hard seam that tears when adjacent
  370:            // bones rotate apart. Splitting each vertex between its own bone and
  371:            // its parent (capped <=4 influences, normalized to 1) lets the seam
  372:            // bend smoothly instead of cracking.
